   "source": [
    "----\n",
    "<div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center;\">\n",
    "    <img src=\"https://developers.lseg.com/content/dam/devportal/icons/logo/lseg-logo.svg\" width=\"20%\" style=\"vertical-align: top;\">\n",
    "    <h1 style=\"margin-left: 20px;\">Data Library for Python</h1>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "----"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Discovery layer - Customers and Suppliers\n",
    "This notebook covers the public `Customers` and `Suppliers` classes exported by `lseg.data.discovery`.,
    "\n",
    "**Prerequisites:** a configured desktop session and entitlement to the underlying relationship and symbol-conversion data. The tests use desktop sessions. Relationships and identifiers change over time; no fixed membership or record count is assumed. Errors are not suppressed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Learn more\n",
    "Visit the [LSEG Developer Portal](https://developers.lseg.com/en) for learning materials.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Getting Help and Support\n",
    "For API questions, visit the [LSEG Developer Community](https://community.developers.lseg.com/).\n",
    "\n",
    "----"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Set the configuration file location\n", "Run this notebook from its own directory. Keep session credentials in `lseg-data.config.json`."]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["import os\n", "\n", "os.environ[\"LD_LIB_CONFIG_PATH\"] = os.path.join(\"..\", \"..\", \"Configuration\")"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Some Imports to start with"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["import lseg.data as ld\n", "from lseg.data.discovery import Customers, Suppliers"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Open the data session\n", "Configure the default session as a desktop session to reproduce the tests."]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["ld.open_session()"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Retrieve customers\n",
    "Construct the object with a company identifier, then call `get_data()` to populate it. This method updates the object and returns `None`: read the result from `.df`, rather than assigning the return value to a DataFrame.\n",
    "\n",
    "The DataFrame includes relationship type, related organization ID, common name, identifiers, confidence and freshness scores, relationship update date, headquarters country, industry and available ratings. Some organizations may not have a quote RIC."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["customers = Customers(\"VOD.L\")\n", "customers.get_data()\n", "customers.df"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Retrieve suppliers\n", "`Suppliers` exposes the same interface; the returned relationship type is `Supplier` instead of `Customer`."]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["suppliers = Suppliers(\"VOD.L\")\n", "suppliers.get_data()\n", "suppliers.df"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Reuse the resolved identifiers\n",
    "After retrieval, `.rics` and `.org_ids` expose available quote and organization identifiers. The tests compare these lists to the populated data. The lists need not have equal lengths because an organization may lack a RIC."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Customer RICs:\", customers.rics)\n",
    "print(\"Customer organization IDs:\", customers.org_ids)\n",
    "print(\"Supplier RICs:\", suppliers.rics)\n",
    "print(\"Supplier organization IDs:\", suppliers.org_ids)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Iterate over relationship objects\n",
    "Both collections support iteration and indexing after `get_data()`. Individual objects expose attributes such as `company_common_name`, `relationship_type`, `related_organization_id`, `ric`, `issue_isin` and relationship scores. This example handles a legitimately empty collection before accessing the first item."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for supplier in suppliers:\n",
    "    print(supplier.company_common_name, supplier.relationship_type, supplier.ric)\n",
    "\n",
    "if customers.df.empty:\n",
    "    print(\"No customers were returned for this instrument.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    first_customer = customers[0]\n",
    "    print(first_customer.company_common_name)\n",
    "    print(first_customer.related_organization_id)\n",
    "    print(first_customer.value_chains_relationship_confidence_score)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Error behavior\n",
    "The tests request `Customers(\"invalid\")` and `Suppliers(\"invalid\")`, then call `get_data()` and expect an `LDError` reporting unresolved identifiers. A failure is not an empty relationship dataset: inspect the exception and the identifier instead of treating an error as an absence of customers or suppliers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Close the session\n", "Run this cell even if an earlier request fails. No server-side resources were created."]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["ld.close_session()"]
  }
 ],
